WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.519 --> 00:00:02.131
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:05.013
Today's message is be present.

00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:06.911
Over to you, Chris Evans.

00:00:06.911 --> 00:00:09.049
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.049 --> 00:00:11.317
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.317 --> 00:00:13.951
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:17.451
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.824 --> 00:00:20.438
- [Interviewer] You said
that there's a search

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:22.371
to be in the moment.

00:00:22.371 --> 00:00:24.309
Does that only apply to acting?

00:00:24.309 --> 00:00:26.284
- It's everything that
reality looks and feels

00:00:26.284 --> 00:00:29.297
and smells and sounds like,
but you know it's not.

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:33.092
And you're completely in
control of that unfolding.

00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:37.130
And that's the time where I
really feel the most present.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.022
And I think that's part
of my addiction to acting,

00:00:39.022 --> 00:00:40.791
because I struggle to find that in life.

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:44.307
It's a bit harder when there's no script,

00:00:44.307 --> 00:00:47.767
and this is just happening
in a chaotic form,

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:50.866
but the hunt for the moment, you know,

00:00:50.866 --> 00:00:53.340
the hunt to be present, that's the goal.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.476
Acting is like a temporary
artificial substance.

00:00:56.476 --> 00:00:59.565
It's like a drug.
It's great.

00:00:59.565 --> 00:01:03.702
My goal in life is to find
that, to be present like that,

00:01:03.702 --> 00:01:05.285
in life, it's hard.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.265
- I think it's super
easy to get distracted

00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:09.625
as an entrepreneur.

00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:11.400
I think entrepreneurs get
distracted all the time.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.050
It prevents you from
accomplishing the big goals

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.454
you want to accomplish.

00:01:14.454 --> 00:01:16.587
I think there's a couple reasons for it.

00:01:16.587 --> 00:01:19.198
I think a lot of entrepreneurs
have ADD diagnosed

00:01:19.198 --> 00:01:20.675
or not diagnosed, we just
tend to like to jump around

00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:22.659
and do a whole bunch of different things.

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:24.760
I think also part of the reasons is

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.825
we don't have a manager,
we don't have a boss.

00:01:26.825 --> 00:01:28.591
When you have a boss that's
telling you what to do,

00:01:28.591 --> 00:01:30.939
who sets guidelines and objectives,

00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:32.175
then you're going to do it,

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:33.824
otherwise you're going to get
in trouble with your manager.

00:01:33.824 --> 00:01:34.931
You might get fired.

00:01:34.931 --> 00:01:36.578
Who's going to fire you?

00:01:36.578 --> 00:01:38.267
You don't fire yourself.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.957
And so you end up letting yourself down.

00:01:39.957 --> 00:01:41.274
You say you're going to do this,

00:01:41.274 --> 00:01:42.712
and then as soon as it gets hard,

00:01:42.712 --> 00:01:43.946
or you lose interest in it,

00:01:43.946 --> 00:01:45.433
you jump to something else.

00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:46.828
As a result, what a lot
of entrepreneurs do,

00:01:46.828 --> 00:01:48.390
is they have all these projects that are

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.871
10, 20, 30, 40, 50% done.

00:01:50.871 --> 00:01:54.080
Look at all the things that
you started and stopped

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.671
and that are kind of sitting
there on the sidelines

00:01:56.671 --> 00:01:58.113
and you've done nothing with.

00:01:58.113 --> 00:01:59.389
It's super common.

00:01:59.389 --> 00:02:00.873
A lot of entrepreneurs do this.

00:02:00.873 --> 00:02:02.481
But you don't get the results.

00:02:02.481 --> 00:02:04.503
You don't get the fruits.

00:02:04.503 --> 00:02:06.441
Unless you take it to 100%.

00:02:06.441 --> 00:02:08.647
You're not going to cash in on something

00:02:08.647 --> 00:02:11.014
that's 50% done, 20% done,
and as soon as something

00:02:11.014 --> 00:02:14.066
gets hard, or as soon
as we hit a roadblock,

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.212
a lot of times what entrepreneurs do is

00:02:16.212 --> 00:02:18.105
they say, I'm not
interested in that anymore.

00:02:18.105 --> 00:02:19.591
That's not what I want to do.

00:02:19.591 --> 00:02:20.743
I'm not passionate about that.

00:02:20.743 --> 00:02:22.521
I'm going to go and do something else.

00:02:22.521 --> 00:02:24.374
Just see if that's your habit.

00:02:24.374 --> 00:02:26.349
See how often you actually follow through,

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:29.073
all the way to completion,
that idea you had

00:02:29.073 --> 00:02:31.546
or that you started, and
when it got hard, you stopped

00:02:31.546 --> 00:02:33.236
and moved on to something else.

00:02:33.236 --> 00:02:35.172
And so the two things that
if ind really helped me

00:02:35.172 --> 00:02:38.516
is one, having a mission, having a vision.

00:02:38.516 --> 00:02:40.408
What do I want to do?
What am I here to do?

00:02:40.408 --> 00:02:41.963
I want to help a billion entrepreneurs.

00:02:41.963 --> 00:02:44.811
I want to have a big
impact on this planet,

00:02:44.811 --> 00:02:47.686
and my path is by
believing in entrepreneurs.

00:02:47.686 --> 00:02:48.958
That's what I want to do.

00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:50.436
I wake up thinking about the impact

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.901
that I want to have today on the planet.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:56.566
What that does is help get
me through a lot of the crap.

00:02:56.566 --> 00:02:59.530
Because being an entrepreneur
is not all roses.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.427
There's a lot of really bad days

00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:03.285
that a lot of people don't talk about.

00:03:03.285 --> 00:03:05.384
When I was writing my book,
there were a lot of bad days,

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:08.391
and what gets me through is
I want to write this book,

00:03:08.391 --> 00:03:10.739
I wanted to inspire lots of entrepreneurs,

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:12.548
I wanted to have an impact.

00:03:12.548 --> 00:03:14.317
And so having a clear mission,

00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:16.702
understanding the bigger
picture, remembering your why

00:03:16.702 --> 00:03:19.217
and what you're doing here,
can help get you through

00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:23.175
that final 50% or maybe
even just the final 10%

00:03:23.175 --> 00:03:27.174
that's just really hard and you
need that extra little kick.

00:03:27.174 --> 00:03:28.450
The second thing that really helps me too

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.756
is having a schedule,
so I know what I'm doing

00:03:30.756 --> 00:03:32.238
every single day of the week.

00:03:32.238 --> 00:03:33.472
I've booked it in.

00:03:33.472 --> 00:03:34.916
One day I'm working on my YouTube channel.

00:03:34.916 --> 00:03:36.602
One day I'm working on
trying to dance salsa.

00:03:36.602 --> 00:03:38.259
One day I'm doing meetings.

00:03:38.259 --> 00:03:40.278
And so I have it set up in my calendar

00:03:40.278 --> 00:03:42.707
that this is what I'm working on today.

00:03:42.707 --> 00:03:44.764
I've allocated the amount
of time that I need

00:03:44.764 --> 00:03:47.312
to go off and have a
big impact in that area

00:03:47.312 --> 00:03:49.209
of my business or my life.

00:03:49.209 --> 00:03:50.442
So those two things.

00:03:50.442 --> 00:03:52.373
Remembering the why and scheduling it in

00:03:52.373 --> 00:03:55.674
helps take those projects
that may be I would dump

00:03:55.674 --> 00:03:59.420
at 50% because I don't
have anybody watching me.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.317
There's no manager holding me accountable.

00:04:01.317 --> 00:04:04.201
And allows me to follow
through and finish to 100%

00:04:04.201 --> 00:04:07.499
so I can get the rewards that I'm after.

00:04:07.499 --> 00:04:09.062
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:04:09.062 --> 00:04:10.586
how do you guys stay present?

00:04:10.586 --> 00:04:12.194
How do you guys stay focused?

00:04:12.194 --> 00:04:13.925
How do you make sure the
projects that you say

00:04:13.925 --> 00:04:16.103
you're going to finish you
actually follow through

00:04:16.103 --> 00:04:17.436
and finish them?

00:04:18.283 --> 00:04:19.396
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:04:19.396 --> 00:04:20.751
Super curious to find out.

00:04:20.751 --> 00:04:22.808
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Caitlin Gag.

00:04:22.808 --> 00:04:24.497
Caitlin, thank you so
much for picking up a copy

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.062
of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:26.062 --> 00:04:27.834
It really really really means a lot to me,

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.728
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:29.728 --> 00:04:31.088
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:31.088 --> 00:04:32.325
I believe in you.

00:04:32.325 --> 00:04:33.976
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:33.976 --> 00:04:35.956
and whatever your one word is,

00:04:35.956 --> 00:04:37.645
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:37.645 --> 00:04:40.984
for another shot of entspresso.

00:04:40.984 --> 00:04:43.041
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:45.801
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:49.385
(manual typewriter clicks)

00:04:49.385 --> 00:04:52.356
- When I'm playing
football, I appreciate it.

00:04:52.356 --> 00:04:54.296
I'm nowhere else.
I'm in the present.

00:04:54.296 --> 00:04:57.768
That's probably the
best part about my life

00:04:57.768 --> 00:04:59.986
is that to be in the
present, you talk about

00:04:59.986 --> 00:05:00.933
how do you enjoy your life?

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.456
How do you find balance, right?

00:05:02.456 --> 00:05:03.570
It's to live in the present.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.014
To live like a kid.

00:05:05.014 --> 00:05:06.577
Like why do kids have so much fun?

00:05:06.577 --> 00:05:09.051
Because they just care
about what they're doing.

00:05:09.051 --> 00:05:09.884
- Yeah.

00:05:09.884 --> 00:05:12.058
- And if we thought about what
we were doing all the time,

00:05:12.058 --> 00:05:13.994
you do that when you're
on the football field.

00:05:13.994 --> 00:05:15.803
It's probably the only
place I can really do that,

00:05:15.803 --> 00:05:18.441
when I really truly am my authentic self.

00:05:18.441 --> 00:05:19.594
I mean, a lot of people see it.

00:05:19.594 --> 00:05:21.736
My close close friends do.

00:05:21.736 --> 00:05:23.969
But when I'm on the football
field, it's just raw.

00:05:23.969 --> 00:05:26.965
- I don't like to think too far ahead.

00:05:26.965 --> 00:05:29.235
I don't like thinking too far ahead.

00:05:29.235 --> 00:05:32.426
People set like goals, long
distance goals and shit.

00:05:32.426 --> 00:05:33.862
That's too much for me.

00:05:33.862 --> 00:05:35.834
I already feel like I'm living it,

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:38.514
and then I just carry
on, carry on day by day,

00:05:38.514 --> 00:05:40.929
already living the final goal,

00:05:40.929 --> 00:05:42.628
the goal of being the world champion.

00:05:42.628 --> 00:05:44.442
I already carry myself
like a world champion.

00:05:44.442 --> 00:05:46.340
I already speak like I'm a world champion.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.382
And that's it.
I just carry on, day by day.

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.156
So I'll take it as it comes.

00:05:51.156 --> 00:05:53.960
Again, like I said, you
asked me about the future.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.677
I'll let you know a little bit closer,

00:05:56.677 --> 00:05:58.083
you know what I mean?

00:05:58.083 --> 00:05:59.855
All I can see right now is the gold.

00:05:59.855 --> 00:06:01.170
That's all I can see.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.534
- Your background is very well documented,

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:05.123
the things you went through,
which have shaped you.

00:06:05.123 --> 00:06:07.359
How much of that is really behind you?

00:06:07.359 --> 00:06:09.210
How much do those ghosts still haunt you?

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:12.671
The involvement in issues
that got you imprisoned

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:16.540
and tortured and, you know,
the drug use and so on?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:19.217
- I am myself and my
circumstances, I think,

00:06:19.217 --> 00:06:22.467
like a Spanish philosopher used to say.

00:06:25.104 --> 00:06:26.085
So who am I?

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:30.255
I am a son of the experiences
that I lived in my life.

00:06:30.255 --> 00:06:32.446
That said, of course, I don't look back,

00:06:32.446 --> 00:06:36.599
because if I look back, I may
become a (mumbles) of thought.

00:06:36.599 --> 00:06:39.045
So I try to live my life here,

00:06:39.045 --> 00:06:42.256
but it is the sum of difficult moments,

00:06:42.256 --> 00:06:46.262
good moments, experiences
that I had in my life,

00:06:46.262 --> 00:06:50.429
that brought me here in front
of this camera talking to you.

00:06:52.153 --> 00:06:56.299
You don't live your life
in this capitalistic sense

00:06:56.299 --> 00:07:00.092
that you accumulate knowledge
as you accumulate money.

00:07:00.092 --> 00:07:01.334
No no no no no.

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:04.078
Life is about the present moment.

00:07:04.078 --> 00:07:08.246
You're here, you're here now,
and then you have an idea

00:07:08.246 --> 00:07:12.384
or have some thing, but that
may be a root in your past,

00:07:12.384 --> 00:07:16.494
but you don't know, so what I
try to do is to live my life

00:07:16.494 --> 00:07:19.161
as full, as intensely, as I can.

